            <ArticleTitle>Urgent coronary artery bypass surgery in the presence of Dressler's syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical features of Dressler's syndrome which developed in a patient following a third myocardial infarction responded to a short course of prednisolone. However, angina at rest precipitated urgent coronary artery bypass surgery and pericardectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
